{\rtf1\ansi\deff0{\fonttbl{\f0 \fswiss Helvetica;}{\f1 \fmodern Courier;}}
{\colortbl;\red255\green0\blue0;\red0\green0\blue255;}
\widowctrl\hyphauto

{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Shows what a MIDI controller actually sends: the shape of the movement over time, one fader bar per active CC, and how fast and how regularly each CC transmits, on each MIDI channel separately.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Two display modes: a scrolling time graph with a labelled axis (1-30 s window) and one bar per active CC with its current value. The same CC on different channels is a separate row, with the same hue and a different shade, and the CC and channel filters combine. Three numbers per row are measured over exactly the last second: Messages (how often the controller sends), Motion (how far the value travels, in CC units/s) and Timing (how much the spacing between messages wobbles). Pointing at them says the same thing on screen.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 The pair list sits below the plot or beside it, for windows that are wide and short. Freeze stops the acquisition while MIDI keeps passing through; Clear wipes history and metrics. The seven parameters are drawn as a control bar instead of REAPER sliders and stay automatable, in presets and under Param.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Written for testing MIDI hardware: the numbers tell you whether a controller really transmits at high resolution, whether its timing is stable, and how hard you are actually moving it. Written for REAPER 6.37 or newer.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Bugs, defined changes and the roadmap live in the repository's issues and discussions, not in the package.\par}
}

{\rtf1\ansi\deff0{\fonttbl{\f0 \fswiss Helvetica;}{\f1 \fmodern Courier;}}
{\colortbl;\red255\green0\blue0;\red0\green0\blue255;}
\widowctrl\hyphauto

{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel0 \b \fs36 REAPER tools\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 My public REAPER tools, published as a {\b ReaPack repository} \u8212- install once, and REAPER keeps them up to date.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel1 \b \fs32 Install\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 In REAPER: {\i Extensions \u8594 ? ReaPack \u8594 ? Import a repository}, paste this URL, then synchronize:\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \f1 https://github.com/solyarisoftware/reaper/raw/master/index.xml\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Manual install, if you prefer: copy the {\f1 .jsfx} {\b and} its {\f1 .jsfx-inc} companions into the same folder inside your REAPER resource directory ({\f1 Effects/<category>/} on Windows).\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel1 \b \fs32 Packages\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 | Package | ReaPack category | What it does | |---|---|---| | {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "MIDI/ccscope/"}}{\fldrslt{\ul
CCScope
}}}
 | {\f1 MIDI/ccscope} | Oscilloscope for MIDI CC: scrolling graph and fader bars, per channel, with performance metrics |\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Each package keeps its documentation next to its sources \u8212- README, changelog, roadmap, screenshot:\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "MIDI/ccscope/"}}{\fldrslt{\ul
{\f1 MIDI/ccscope/}
}}}
 \u8212- {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "MIDI/ccscope/README.md"}}{\fldrslt{\ul
README
}}}
 \u183 ? {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "MIDI/ccscope/CHANGELOG.md"}}{\fldrslt{\ul
changelog
}}}
 \u183 ? {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "MIDI/ccscope/TODO.md"}}{\fldrslt{\ul
roadmap
}}}
\sa180\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel1 \b \fs32 How this repository is organised\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 This is a ReaPack repository, so {\b the folder tree is the package taxonomy}: a file in {\f1 MIDI/ccscope/} is installed as {\f1 Effects/MIDI/ccscope/<file>} and appears under the {\i MIDI/ccscope} category in ReaPack. The {\f1 index.xml} at the root is generated from the files' metadata headers by {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://github.com/cfillion/reapack-index"}}{\fldrslt{\ul
reapack-index
}}}
 running in GitHub Actions \u8212- do not edit it by hand.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Each package lives in its own folder, with everything it needs: the sources, the includes it imports (which resolve relative to it), and its own documentation.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel1 \b \fs32 Feedback and contributions\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab {\b Bug:} open an issue with reproduction steps and expected versus actual behaviour.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab {\b Idea or workflow need:} start a discussion in {\b Ideas}.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab {\b Defined feature or change request:} open an enhancement issue with completion criteria.\sa180\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Start titles with the tool name, such as {\f1 CCScope - \u8230 ?}. Open topics are not promises of implementation or delivery dates. Testing, documentation and code contributions are welcome.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Full guidelines: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "CONTRIBUTING.md"}}{\fldrslt{\ul
CONTRIBUTING.md
}}}
.\par}
