{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel1 \b \fs32 Support\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 {\b IF YOU LIKE THE PROJECT, PLEASE \u11088 ?\u65039 ?STAR THIS REPOSITORY TO SHOW YOUR SUPPORT!}\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 A star costs nothing, and it is the only signal GitHub shows to whoever is looking for a tool like this one: the count is what makes a repository look alive.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 If you want to go further, there is a donate button in the {\b Sponsor} menu of this repository:\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab {\b {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.paypal.com/donate/?hosted_button_id=AEV3EVJEUFM32"}}{\fldrslt{\ul
Donate with PayPal
}}}
}\sa180\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Donations are entirely voluntary and help cover investigation, development, testing and documentation. You do not need to donate to report a bug, propose an improvement or join a discussion. A donation does not guarantee implementation, priority, a delivery date or support. It is not a purchase: nothing is unlocked and nothing changes in the license. The minimum is 5 EUR, for a practical reason \u8212- below that the PayPal fee takes most of it. The same button funds the other open-source work of mine (dxconvey, the scale collections), so one pointer covers all of it.\par}
